  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 22d0308a90dc49ae97395f1b651723b5, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q_CTX_08_DiscoveryShortcut
  questionId: CTX-08
  category: 0
  speakerName: Hiring Manager
  questionText: >-
    The account executive says discovery is already done and asks you to just run the executive demo. The first slide makes that seem optimistic. What do you do?
  answerOptions:
  - {fileID: 11400001}
  - {fileID: 11400002}
  - {fileID: 11400003}
  - {fileID: 11400004}
--- !u!114 &11400001
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0d521c6b84db4b8fae30e3785d9e9582, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q_CTX_08_A1
  answerText: >-
    Open with two validation questions, explain they will make the demo shorter, and then tailor live.
  technicalDelta: 1
  commercialDelta: 2
  rapportDelta: 1
  energyDelta: 0
--- !u!114 &11400002
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0d521c6b84db4b8fae30e3785d9e9582, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q_CTX_08_A2
  answerText: >-
    Trust the account executive and give the standard executive demo with confidence.
  technicalDelta: -1
  commercialDelta: 1
  rapportDelta: 0
  energyDelta: 1
--- !u!114 &11400003
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0d521c6b84db4b8fae30e3785d9e9582, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q_CTX_08_A3
  answerText: >-
    Stop and say discovery was clearly not done, then ask to restart the meeting.
  technicalDelta: 1
  commercialDelta: -1
  rapportDelta: -3
  energyDelta: -1
--- !u!114 &11400004
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0d521c6b84db4b8fae30e3785d9e9582, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q_CTX_08_A4
  answerText: >-
    Name the assumption risk, ask the executive to pick the business outcome, and skip anything that does not support it.
  technicalDelta: 0
  commercialDelta: 3
  rapportDelta: 1
  energyDelta: -1
